### MINOR-9 — `.changes/README.md` scope vocabulary is copied from devin-telegram.

`.changes/README.md` lists `scope` values `cli, daemon, state, acp, mailbox, wake, ingress,
tooling, docs, deploy` — a module taxonomy that does not exist in this repository
(no `cli`/`daemon`/`state`/`acp`/`mailbox`/`wake`/`ingress` packages; the actual tree is
`domain`/`contract`/`adapters`/`tooling`/`docs`/`deploy`). Fragments written against this
list carry meaningless scopes.

### MINOR-10 — `.devin/roadmap.md` is absent.

`.windsurfrules` mandates that the root session maintain `.devin/roadmap.md`; the file does
not exist (`.devin/` contains `project.json`, `config.json`, `cycle_log.jsonl`, `agents/`,
`scripts/` only). The audit item "read `.devin/roadmap.md`" resolves to: nothing to review.
Infra inconsistency, not a code defect.

### MINOR-11 — `LineSummary.liveness` defaults to `REACHABLE` for unbound lines.

`contract.py` `LineSummary` (`liveness` default `LivenessState.REACHABLE`): a line with no
provider binding reads as healthy on the health axis; `caps == ()` is the only signal that
nothing is attached. Documented choice, but a consumer keying "line is usable" off
`liveness` alone is misled — worth one sentence in the docstring or a derived
`UNREACHABLE`-for-unbound convention.

### MINOR-12 — `admin.assign_line` is not explicitly barred from minting a `system:*` owner.

`SYSTEM_AGENT_PREFIX`/`is_system_agent` (`contract.py:372-391`) and the external-socket
rejection (`contract.py:3220-3227`, api-contract.md:111/210) cover `agent_id` at
`register_intent` and the API-key issuance rule. `LineAssignment.owner_agent_id` is
`_CheckedAgentId`, which deliberately *permits* `system:*` internally (needed for the
fallback worker session). But `assign_line(line_id, owner_agent_id)` (admin surface,
`contract.py:3968+`) never states that a `system:*` owner is rejected — a durable exclusive
assignment owned by `system:anything` is constructible through the admin path. Trusted
surface, so Minor; one docstring line closes it.

