## 5. Bottom line

The v0.0.20 consolidation is in good shape: every previously-remediated item in the audit
brief verified as correctly specified or correctly modeled, and all gates (pytest 80,
ruff, mypy, spec anchors, version tag, changes entry) pass. Two items deserve closure
before M1 begins rather than after: the missing `name`↔payload binding on `EventEnvelope`
(MAJOR-1 — one model validator plus a lookup table) and the transitive-forward-cycle
requirement that exists only in the spec/docs but not in the contract docstrings
(MAJOR-2 — docstring amendment; the enforcement lands in M1). The Minor set is dominated
by docstring lag and consistency gaps, plus two genuine specification holes in the
reregister/reissue race (MINOR-6/7) that should be pinned now while the semantics are
still cheap to state.
